('practice-11-paper','math',1,10,'A cable provider wanted to know how many of its
   30, 000 customers would be interested in a new
   service plan. The provider selected 300 customers at
   random and asked each customer whether the
   customer would be interested in the new plan. Of
   those surveyed, 8 said they would be interested.
  Which of the following is the best estimate of the
    total number of customers who would be interested
   in the new service plan?
  A)  8
   B)  80
   C) 800
  D)  ,8 000','Escolha a melhor alternativa para a questão reproduzida na imagem.','[{"key": "A", "text": "8"}, {"key": "B", "text": "80"}, {"key": "C", "text": "800"}, {"key": "D", "text": ",8 000"}]'::jsonb,'multiple-choice',ARRAY['C']::text[],'Choice C is correct. It’s given that 8 out of 300 customers in a random sample said they would be interested in the new plan. This means the fraction of sampled customers who said they would be interested is 300 8 . Multiplying this fraction by the total customer population yields , 30 000 300 8 a ^k h, or 800. Therefore, the best estimate of the total number of customers who would be interested in the new service plan is 800.','/sat-assets/practice-11/math-m1-q10.png','https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/sat-practice-test-11-digital.pdf',36,'published'),
