     -7 +  k   x =                  , where k is a constant. What is the          2
   value of k?','Digite sua resposta para a questão reproduzida na imagem.','[]'::jsonb,'numeric',ARRAY['29']::text[],'The correct answer is 29. The solutions to a quadratic equation in the form ax bx c 0 2 + + = , where a, b, and c are constants, can be calculated using the quadratic formula, which gives two solutions: x a b b ac 2 4 2 = - + - and x a b b ac 2 4 2 = - - - . The given equation is in the form ax bx c 0 2 + + = , where a 1 = , b 7 = , and c 5 = . It follows that one solution to the given quadratic equation is x 2 1 7 7 4 1 5 2 = - + - ] ] ] g g g, or x 2 7 49 20 = - + - , which is equivalent to x 2 7 29 = - + . It’s given that one solution to the given equation can be written as x k 2 7 = - + , where k is a constant. It follows that the value of k is 29.','/sat-assets/practice-11/math-m1-q21.png','https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/sat-practice-test-11-digital.pdf',39,'published'),
('practice-11-paper','math',1,22,'A scientist measured the lengths of 240 gray seals
   from Muskeget Island and 120 gray seals from Sable
   Island. The scientist determined that the mean
   length of the 240 gray seals from Muskeget Island
   was 88 inches and the mean length of the 120 gray
    seals from Sable Island was 94 inches. What was the
  mean length of all 360 gray seals the scientist
   measured for this study?
  A)  89
   B)  90
   C) 91
  D) 92','Escolha a melhor alternativa para a questão reproduzida na imagem.','[{"key": "A", "text": "89"}, {"key": "B", "text": "90"}, {"key": "C", "text": "91"}, {"key": "D", "text": "92"}]'::jsonb,'multiple-choice',ARRAY['B']::text[],'Choice B is correct. The mean of a data set is calculated by dividing the sum of the values in the data set by the number of values in the data set. It’s given that the mean length of the 240 gray seals from Muskeget Island was 88 inches. This can be represented by the equation x 88 240 = , where x represents the sum of the lengths, in inches, of the 240 gray seals from Muskeget Island. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 240 yields x 240 88 = ^ ^h h, or , x 21 120 = inches. It’s also given that the mean length of the 120 gray seals from Sable Island was 94 inches. This can be represented by the equation y 94 120 = , where y represents the sum of the lengths, in inches, of the 120 gray seals from Sable Island. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 120 yields y 120 94 = ^ ^h h, or , y 11 280 = inches. Therefore, the sum of the lengths, in inches, of all 360 gray seals is , , 21 120 11 280 + , or , 32 400. Dividing this sum by 360 yields , 360 32 400, or 90 inches. Therefore, the mean length of all 360 gray seals the scientist measured for this study is 90 inches.','/sat-assets/practice-11/math-m1-q22.png','https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/sat-practice-test-11-digital.pdf',39,'published'),
